# Stray copies of a tracked file — the artifact a file manager or an editor
# leaves behind when a file is duplicated: "name - Copy" (Windows/VS Code,
# second duplicate "name - Copy (2)"), "name copy" (macOS, "name copy 2"),
# "name (copy)" (GNOME Nautilus, "name (another copy)", "name (3rd copy)"),
# "Copy of name" (JetBrains IDEs, second duplicate "Copy of name (1)").
# A copy is never a source: it silently drifts from the file it duplicates.
# The pipeline gate
# (tests/config-validator/__tests__/stray-copy-artifacts.test.js) fails the
# build if one is ever tracked anyway.
#
# The marker is reserved: a file that legitimately carries one (a real source
# called "deep copy.js") must be renamed, not forced in — `git add -f` gets it
# past this layer and straight into the gate. Negation rules further down this
# file win over these (last match wins), so a fixture that legitimately needs
# a copy-shaped name can negate it — the pipeline gate still flags it.
* - Copy
* - Copy.*
* - Copy ([0-9]*
* - Copy [0-9]*
* copy
* copy.*
* copy ([0-9]*
* copy [0-9]*
*copy)
*copy).*
*copy) ([0-9]*
*copy) [0-9]*
Copy of *

# Temporary files
*.tmp
.tmp/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

